        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Cairo</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">969 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">969, when the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mu'izz li-Din Allah had his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawhar-al-siqilli">Jawhar</a> al-Saqili build a new fortified city northeast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fustat">Fustat</a>; the caliph arrived in 973 and gave it its name</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and two islands in it, just south of the point where the river leaves its desert valley and branches into the Delta, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fustat">Fustat</a> and the Fatimid foundation of al-Qahira; al-Azhar; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s Citadel; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultans' mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-death">Black Death</a> of 1348; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo-geniza">Cairo Geniza</a>; Isma'il's Downtown; Tahrir Square</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Cairo is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, with a metropolitan area of more than 22 million people.</span></div>
